    "top_keyword_score": 0.5333333333333333,
    "top_section": "THIRD-PARTY VENDOR MANAGEMENT",
    "retrieval_seconds": 0.2910275210015243,
    "answer_seconds": 5.2893368450022535,
    "total_seconds": 5.580384571992909,
    "answer": "Before engagement and approval:\n\n1. Business owner submits a Vendor Request Form in ServiceNow.\n2. Procurement reviews commercial terms and pricing, including SLA, insurance, and liability.\n3. Security conducts an assessment using the standardized questionnaire appropriate to criticality.\n4. Legal reviews the data processing agreement (DPA) and contract terms.\n5. The DPO reviews and approves the DPA because the vendor handles personal data.\n6. The transfer outside the EEA must use SCCs, an adequacy decision, or BCRs, and the DPO must approve the transfer at **dpo@acme.com**.\n7. The CISO signs off because the vendor is classified as High risk.\n\nAfter approval, the vendor is onboarded and added to the Approved Vendor Registry.\n\n**Sections: THIRD-PARTY VENDOR MANAGEMENT; DATA PRIVACY AND GDPR COMPLIANCE**",
